          simpleExplanation: '• Public Key Cryptography: Key pair (Public key shared openly, Private key kept secret).\n• Diffie-Hellman Key Exchange: Allows two parties to establish a shared secret over an insecure channel: Shared Key K = (Y_B)^X_A mod q = (Y_A)^X_B mod q. Vulnerable to Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) if unauthenticated.\n• RSA Algorithm:\n  1. Pick two large prime numbers p and q.\n  2. Compute modulus n = p * q, and Euler Totient phi(n) = (p - 1) * (q - 1).\n  3. Choose public exponent e such that gcd(e, phi(n)) = 1 and 1 < e < phi(n).\n  4. Compute private key d = e^-1 mod phi(n) (d * e ≡ 1 mod phi(n)).\n  5. Encryption: C = M^e mod n. Decryption: M = C^d mod n.',
