          simpleExplanation: '• Vanishing Gradient Problem: Deep networks me Sigmoid/Tanh derivatives (< 0.25) baar-baar multiply hone par zero ho jate hain, jisse shuruati layers ke weights update hona band ho jate hain.\n• Activation Functions:\n  - Sigmoid: σ(z) = 1 / (1 + e^-z) -> (0, 1), suffers from vanishing gradients.\n  - Tanh: (-1, 1), zero-centered.\n  - ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit): f(x) = max(0, x) -> Solves vanishing gradient, fast calculation.\n  - Leaky ReLU: f(x) = max(0.01x, x) -> Solves "Dying ReLU" problem.\n  - Softmax: Converts vector of logits into a probability distribution summing to 1.0.',
          keyFormulasOrKeywords: ['ReLU: f(x) = max(0, x)', 'Softmax: e^zi / sum(e^zj)', 'Vanishing Gradient solved by ReLU & Residual connections'],
