          simpleExplanation: '• Standard RNN: Loops information over sequential time steps (h_t = tanh(W*h_{t-1} + U*x_t)). Suffers from Exploding & Vanishing Gradients over long sequences.\n• Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) Architecture:\n  - Cell State (C_t): Long-term memory highway.\n  - 1. Forget Gate (f_t): Decides what information to discard: f_t = sigma(W_f * [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_f).\n  - 2. Input Gate (i_t): Decides what new information to store in cell state: i_t = sigma(W_i * [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_i).\n  - 3. Output Gate (o_t): Decides output hidden state h_t: o_t = sigma(W_o * [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_o); h_t = o_t * tanh(C_t).\n• Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU): Simplified LSTM with only 2 gates (Reset and Update gates).',
