          simpleExplanation: '• Why Transformers: Overcomes RNN sequential bottleneck; processes all tokens in parallel via Self-Attention.\n• Scaled Dot-Product Attention Formula:\n  Attention(Q, K, V) = softmax( (Q * K^T) / sqrt(d_k) ) * V\n  - Query (Q): What am I looking for?\n  - Key (K): What do I contain?\n  - Value (V): What content do I offer?\n  - Scaling by sqrt(d_k) prevents large dot products from saturating softmax gradients.\n• Multi-Head Attention: Runs multiple attention mechanisms in parallel, allowing model to attend to information from different representation subspaces.\n• Positional Encoding: Sinusoidal waves injected into embeddings to inject token sequence order.',
